  "deathBeat": [
   "d18: 📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Karen Guenther is dead. You didn't ask. It knew.",
   "d18: 🕯️ Karen Guenther is dead — starvation. The village stops. Somebody screams. Somebody else starts digging.",
   "d18: 📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Sean is dead. You didn't ask. It knew."
  ],
  "recoverHome": [
   "d19: That night, they bring Karen home. Nobody asks you to help carry; nobody has to. By morning the grave is dug by the fire, and the body is laid out beside it. The filling of it is yours."
  ],
  "vouch": [],
  "systemVoice": [
   "d18: 📺 SYSTEM: \"We have already cleared your morning. You are welcome. We require 300 kcal of tubers and your full attention. The fans love a cooking segment.\""
  ],
  "burialWindowSay": [
   "d19: That night, they bring Karen home. Nobody asks you to help carry; nobody has to. By morning the grave is dug by the fire, and the body is laid out beside it. The filling of it is yours.",
   "d21: You say a few words for Karen. Not a ceremony — just: you were here, and someone noticed you leaving. (-3 trauma)",
   "d21: Burying the bloating dead was honest work, and it cost you. Fever by nightfall. (-10 health)",
   "d21: You bury Karen. A marker, of sorts. The village will know where. (+4 trauma)"
  ],
